Fix the non-JSON-serialization AOT warnings in the project at `/tmp/sv-95588f6762fe44489465dec9ce9add94/before/`. Make the following changes:

## 1. GenericOperationSource.cs
Add `[DynamicallyAccessedMembers]` to the type parameter `T` on the class `GenericOperationSource<T>`. The `T` is used with `ModelReaderWriter.Read(data, typeof(T))` (needs `PublicConstructors | NonPublicConstructors`) and `Activator.CreateInstance(typeof(T), ...)` (needs `NonPublicConstructors`). So add:

```csharp
internal class GenericOperationSource<[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.PublicConstructors | DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)] T> : IOperationSource<T>
```

Make sure the `using System.Diagnostics.CodeAnalysis;` is present (it already is).

## 2. ArmOperation.cs (at `/tmp/sv-95588f6762fe44489465dec9ce9add94/before/ArmOperation.cs`)
The `IsResource<T>()` method uses `typeof(T).GetConstructor(...)` and `Activator.CreateInstance(typeof(T), ...)`. Add `[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)]` to the `T` type parameter on `IsResource<T>()`.

This will cascade to callers `Rehydrate<T>` and `RehydrateAsync<T>`. Add the same annotation to their `T` type parameters too. Both methods already have `where T : notnull` constraint.

Add `using System.Diagnostics.CodeAnalysis;` if not present.

The resulting signatures should look like:
```csharp
public static ArmOperation<T> Rehydrate<[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)] T>(ArmClient client, RehydrationToken rehydrationToken, ArmClientOptions options = null) where T : notnull
```
```csharp
public static async Task<ArmOperation<T>> RehydrateAsync<[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)] T>(ArmClient client, RehydrationToken rehydrationToken, ArmClientOptions options = null) where T : notnull
```
```csharp
private static bool IsResource<[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)] T>() where T : notnull
```

## 3. ArmClientBuilderExtensions.cs
The method `AddArmClient<TBuilder, TConfiguration>` calls `RegisterClientFactory` which has `[RequiresUnreferencedCode]` and `[RequiresDynamicCode]`. Add both attributes to the method:

```csharp
[RequiresUnreferencedCode("Binding strongly typed objects to configuration values is not supported with trimming.")]
[RequiresDynamicCode("Binding strongly typed objects to configuration values requires generating dynamic code at runtime.")]
public static IAzureClientBuilder<ArmClient, ArmClientOptions> AddArmClient<TBuilder, TConfiguration>(...)
```

Add `using System.Diagnostics.CodeAnalysis;` if not present (it already is).

## 4. Four *ArmOperation files with ToObjectFromJson
These files all have this pattern on line 61:
```csharp
var lroDetails = ModelReaderWriter.Write(rehydrationToken, ModelReaderWriterOptions.Json, AzureResourceManagerContext.Default).ToObjectFromJson<Dictionary<string, string>>();
```

`ToObjectFromJson<T>()` uses JsonSerializer internally and is marked `[RequiresUnreferencedCode]`. Replace with manual `JsonDocument` parsing:

```csharp
var lroData = ModelReaderWriter.Write(rehydrationToken, ModelReaderWriterOptions.Json, AzureResourceManagerContext.Default);
using var lroDoc = JsonDocument.Parse(lroData);
var lroDetails = new Dictionary<string, string>();
foreach (var prop in lroDoc.RootElement.EnumerateObject())
{
    lroDetails[prop.Name] = prop.Value.GetString();
}
```

The four files are:
- `/tmp/sv-95588f6762fe44489465dec9ce9add94/before/ManagementGroup/Generated/LongRunningOperation/ManagementGroupsArmOperation.cs`
- `/tmp/sv-95588f6762fe44489465dec9ce9add94/before/ManagementGroup/Generated/LongRunningOperation/ManagementGroupsArmOperationOfT.cs`
- `/tmp/sv-95588f6762fe44489465dec9ce9add94/before/Resources/Generated/LongRunningOperation/ResourcesArmOperation.cs`
- `/tmp/sv-95588f6762fe44489465dec9ce9add94/before/Resources/Generated/LongRunningOperation/ResourcesArmOperationOfT.cs`

Make sure `using System.Text.Json;` is present in each file.

## 5. ArmEnvironment.cs
Line 80: `public override string ToString() => JsonSerializer.Serialize(this);`

The `ArmEnvironment` is a simple struct with `Endpoint` (Uri) and `Audience` (string) properties. Replace with manual serialization that produces the same JSON output:

```csharp
public override string ToString()
{
    using var stream = new System.IO.MemoryStream();
    using (var writer = new Utf8JsonWriter(stream))
    {
        writer.WriteStartObject();
        writer.WriteString("Endpoint", Endpoint.ToString());
        writer.WriteString("Audience", Audience);
        writer.WriteEndObject();
    }
    return BinaryData.FromBytes(stream.ToArray()).ToString();
}
```

Check the ArmEnvironment struct properties to make sure you serialize all public properties. Look at the file to understand the struct.

## 6. ArmClientOptions.cs
Line 52: `var allProfile = JsonSerializer.Deserialize<Dictionary<string, Dictionary<string, JsonElement>>>(span);`

Replace with manual JsonDocument parsing:
```csharp
using var profileDoc = JsonDocument.Parse(BinaryData.FromBytes(span.ToArray()));
var allProfile = new Dictionary<string, Dictionary<string, JsonElement>>();
foreach (var section in profileDoc.RootElement.EnumerateObject())
{
    var innerDict = new Dictionary<string, JsonElement>();
    foreach (var inner in section.Value.EnumerateObject())
    {
        innerDict[inner.Name] = inner.Value.Clone();
    }
    allProfile[section.Name] = innerDict;
}
```

Note: The `span` variable is a `ReadOnlySpan<byte>` from `BinaryData.FromStream(stream).ToMemory().Span`. You need to convert to a form that JsonDocument.Parse accepts. Check the exact type and adjust accordingly.

Make sure `using System.Text.Json;` is present.

IMPORTANT: Use the `edit` tool with `old_str`/`new_str` for all changes. Do NOT use `create`. Read each file first before editing to ensure you have the exact strings.

